      "message": "\u003e cec_gpio_interrupt looks generic. It works for any cec driver which needs to translate a gpio pin to a cec port index, doesn\u0027t it?\n\nport_from_gpio_in() is not generic because it gets the gpio from bitbang_cec_config. cec_update_interrupt_time() and cec_event_cap() are also specific to the bitbang driver. If we move it to common it won\u0027t even build because it\u0027s missing these functions/structs. Am I missing something?\n\n\u003e Return 0 from port_from_timer and port_from_gpio_in.\n\nDone.\n\n\u003e If a port index passed to cec_init_timer, can we disable its interrupt to gracefully disable the port?\n\nSorry I still don\u0027t understand, could you share a code snippet? If port is invalid, then cec_config[port].drv_config.timer is an out-of-bounds access. So how would we get the timer to disable?\n\nAlso just to be clear, the port in cec_init_timer() comes from the for loop in https://crrev.com/c/4659322. So the only way for it to be invalid is a bug in that common code (not e.g. incorrect configuration in board code).",
